 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>“We ask not that the slave should lie,<br>\nAs lies his master, at his ease,<br>\nBeneath a silken canopy,<br>\nOr in the shade of blooming trees.</p>\n\n<p>We ask not “eye for eye,” that all<br>\nWho forge the chain and ply the whip<br>\nShould feel their torture, while the thrall<br>\nShould wield the scourge of mastership.</p>\n\n<p>We mourn not that the man should toil.<br>\n'Tis nature's need. 'Tis God's decree.<br>\nBut let the hand that tills the soil<br>\nBe, like the wind that fans it, free.<br>\nMelody—to ‘Old Hundred’ Hymn”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">The Abolitionist Hymn<br>\n(Author unknown, circa 1850s)</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided.</i></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 615524,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A historian might use this song as evidence to support",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1170068,
     "content_html": "the way a lack of copyright and patent precedent led to widespread violations\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170069,
     "content_html": "the role religious affiliation played in the spread of abolitionist sentiment\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170067,
     "content_html": "the popular appeal of Stephen Douglas in the 1860 presidential election\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170066,
     "content_html": "the impact of Irish immigration on the Free Soil movement\n"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 615525,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which group would most likely support the song’s point of view?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1170072,
     "content_html": "Radical abolitionists such as John Brown\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170071,
     "content_html": "Advocates of free black repatriation to the African state of Liberia\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170070,
     "content_html": "Members of the Free Soil party\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170073,
     "content_html": "Antislavery advocates such as Harriet Beecher Stowe\n"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
